<section class="section install-section" id="install" aria-labelledby="install-title">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="section-kicker"><span aria-hidden="true">02</span> Install · one command</p>
    <h2 id="install-title">Summon the guild.</h2>
    <p>
      Questmancer is a Herdr plugin, and Herdr installs it for you. It fetches
      the repository, reads the plugin manifest and downloads a checksummed
      binary for your platform. No clone, no Rust toolchain.
    </p>
  </div>
  <p class="install-prerequisite">
    <span class="install-prerequisite-label">Prerequisite</span>
    Install Herdr first:
    <a href="https://herdr.dev/docs/install/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
      Herdr install guide <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
    </a>
  </p>
  <div class="terminal" aria-label="Questmancer source installation commands">
    <div class="terminal-bar" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="terminal-dot"></span><span class="terminal-dot"></span><span class="terminal-dot"></span>
      <span class="terminal-label">questmancer / install</span>
    </div>
    <pre><code><span class="prompt">$</span> herdr plugin install opsydyn/herdr-questmancer
<span class="prompt">$</span> herdr plugin action invoke opsydyn.questmancer.open</code></pre>
  </div>
  <details class="install-source">
    <summary>Building from source</summary>
    <p>
      For working on Questmancer rather than using it. Herdr links a plugin by
      directory, so it needs the manifest and scripts beside the binary.
    </p>
    <div class="terminal" aria-label="Questmancer source build commands">
      <div class="terminal-bar" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="terminal-dot"></span><span class="terminal-dot"></span><span class="terminal-dot"></span>
        <span class="terminal-label">questmancer / source</span>
      </div>
      <pre><code><span class="prompt">$</span> git clone https://github.com/opsydyn/herdr-questmancer
<span class="prompt">$</span> cd herdr-questmancer
<span class="prompt">$</span> cargo build --release
<span class="prompt">$</span> herdr plugin link .</code></pre>
    </div>
  </details>
</section>
